# data/*.json IS committed, deliberately. The site is served straight from this
# repository by GitHub Pages, so anything not committed does not exist on the
# live app - and without the play files both replays are dead. What is published
# is a heavy derivation rather than either source: one passage of play each,
# resampled to 10 Hz, with names and squad numbers stripped by tools/anonymise.py.
# Attribution is in NOTICE, in the replay caption and in the info sheet.
#
# The raw tracking sources are a different matter and stay out - see below.

# Build inputs that are not ours to redistribute. tools/README.md says where to
# fetch them; the scripts refuse to run without them.
tools/*.csv

# Build by-products. tools/ is where the generators write; the copies the app
# actually serves are the ones in the root, and those are committed.
tools/field.jpg
tools/field_landscape.jpg
tools/pitch.jpg
tools/midfield_preview.png
tools/play.json
tools/soccer.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Scratch
*.log
_*.html

# Chrome profiles and screenshots from headless verification runs
p_*/
*.png.bak
